 equation $Ax=0$ and express the solution as a linear combination of linearly independent vectors. Those vectors form a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\nSince $A∼B,$ the equation $Ax=0$ is equivalent to the equation $Bx=0,$ which corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis implies that the only solution of $Ax=0$ is $x=0.$ So, $\\text{Null}(A)={0},$ which means that the basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ is the empty set, i.e., $B={\\,}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-75017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bc264429e4f25b6e170cfaf2a0df06ead3b3411fb1957d5ecd420df18f600a71"} {"question" "q-75017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-75017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={\\,}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-75017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "B={\\,}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-34522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrices $A$ and $B$ are given below. Given that $A$ is row equivalent to $B$, then find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-34522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A),$ we need to solve the equation $Ax=0$ and express the solution as a linear combination of linearly independent vectors. Those vectors form a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\nSince $A∼B,$ the equation $Ax=0$ is equivalent to the equation $Bx=0,$ which corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is ${x}_{1}=-{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=0,$ where ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThis implies that \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-34522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bc264429e4f25b6e170cfaf2a0df06ead3b3411fb1957d5ecd420df18f600a71"} {"question" "q-34522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-34522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={\\,}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-34522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-111509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$, find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-111509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reduce the matrix $A$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=0$ is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution is ${x}_{1}=-{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}=0,$ where ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThis implies that \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-111509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bc264429e4f25b6e170cfaf2a0df06ead3b3411fb1957d5ecd420df18f600a71"} {"question" "q-111509" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-111509" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={\\,}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-111509" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-34422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}]$, find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-34422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reduce the matrix $A$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=0$ is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution is ${x}_{1}=-{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=0,$ where ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThis implies that \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-34422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bc264429e4f25b6e170cfaf2a0df06ead3b3411fb1957d5ecd420df18f600a71"} {"question" "q-34422" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-34422" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-34422" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-75026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$, find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-75026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reduce the matrix $A$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, equation $Ax=0$ is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}+2{x}_{4}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}-{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution is ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{3}-2{x}_{4}$ and ${x}_{2}=-5{x}_{3}+{x}_{4},$ where ${x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are free variables. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3}-2{x}_{4} \\\\ -5{x}_{3}+{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3} \\\\ -5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{4} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3},{x}_{4}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis implies that \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-75026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bc264429e4f25b6e170cfaf2a0df06ead3b3411fb1957d5ecd420df18f600a71"} {"question" "q-75026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-75026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={\\,}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-75026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "B={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-75024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}]$, find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-75024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reduce the matrix $A$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=0$ is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{3}+2{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution is ${x}_{1}=4{x}_{3}-2{x}_{4},$ where ${x}_{2},$ ${x}_{3},$ and ${x}_{4}$ are free variables. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3}-2{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{4} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis implies that \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fd059646fee128a0be8d4870e075778d91b477e7aaf1cde6772706b029726e6"} {"question" "q-75024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bc2644